-- title:
--   Unramifiedness at vertical height-one primes over the X₀(M') floor
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, $M'\ne 0$ a natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $L$ a field of characteristic zero, algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ together with a ring embedding $L\to\mathbb{C}$ carrying $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $K$ be the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup $H=\ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\big)$, and let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, uniformiser $\varpi$, and an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with the tower $A\to L\to K$. Let $j\in K$ have Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), $j\ne 0$. Let $W_0\subseteq K$ be the valuation subring consisting of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f\cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ (the Gauss ring of $A$-integral $q$-expansions). Let $z$ be a point of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two chart spectra over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$) at whose stalk the germ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ through the structure morphism to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ lies in the maximal ideal, so $z$ lies in the special fibre; assume $z$ is the image under $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ of a point $y$ of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin A K j`, the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$, whose prime is maximal. Assume further an algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A K j` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$ such that $\varphi(j)\notin$ `ssJSet q Ω`, i.e. some elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has a nonzero $q$-torsion point; and that every $b$ in `chartAlgFin A K j` whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$ lies in the prime of $y$. Let $K_0$ be the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (Gamma0 M')`, with $K_0\le K$, with a compatible $A$-algebra structure, and $j_0\in K_0$ nonzero with the same Laurent expansion as $j$; let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from `chartAlgFin A K₀ j₀` to `chartAlgFin A K j` inducing the inclusion $K_0\subseteq K$ on underlying elements. Then, for the algebra structure given by $\iota$, every prime ideal $\mathfrak Q$ of `chartAlgFin A K j` contained in the prime of $y$, of height $1$, and containing the image of $\varpi$, satisfies `Algebra.IsUnramifiedAt` over `chartAlgFin A K₀ j₀`.
--
--   The height-one primes over $(\varpi)$ contained in the maximal ideal at $z$ are the branches of the special fibre of the integral model through $z$; the assertion is that at an ordinary point lying on the branch cut out by the Gauss valuation ring $W_0$ each such branch is unramified over the corresponding branch of the floor $X_0(M')$. It is used in the proof that the fibre ring at such a point is a regular local ring.
